{"activity_text": "Antiviral", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (57.14%) to Brevinin-2CE Activity: The peptide is virucidal against both Zika virus (ZIKV) (D=L) and dengue viruses (DENV). Yodha peptide efficiently inhibited DENV1 (IC50 25 uM), DENV2 (IC50 2 uM), DENV3 (IC50 70 uM), and DENV4 (IC50 30 uM). In vitro toxicity: not hemo.lytic at 160 uM to human RBC. Animal model:mouse: C57BL/6: D-Yodha was IP injected 5 h before infection in the footpad with 100,000 focus forming units of ZIKV strain PRVABC. After peptide injection daily for 3 days, viral load was reduced.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33436917", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Sci Rep. 2021 Jan 12;11(1):602. doi: 10.1038/s41598-020-80596-4. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03332", "source_id": "AP03332", "source_numeric_id": "03332", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03332", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The amphibian peptide Yodha is virucidal for Zika and dengue viruses.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
